Link: https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/security/findings/58dd38b38f808191940211f4bc789ddd?sev=&repo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fjustincormack%2Fargmin
Criticality: low (attack path: low)
Status: fixed

# Resolution
Fixed in commit [`ceadc0a3`](https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/ceadc0a30ecf07209dd13e12ae3043a714c70dc6) (`Reject invalid active primary heartbeat proofs`).

The finding was valid for the reported commit `9123ccc`: invalid Active observations from the current PG primary were filtered out by `should_record_pg_heartbeat_observation`, which let the heartbeat continue, renew the node lease, and potentially receive a lease-bearing Active handoff route on refresh.

The fix moved active-primary metadata safety checks into `validate_pg_heartbeat_observations`, before heartbeat mutation. When the reporting node is the Active primary for the PG, a pending metadata command now hard-fails the heartbeat, and a below-floor/divergent metadata proof returns `PgActiveMetadataProofMismatch`. The old boolean drop/filter helper was removed, so accepted observations are recorded directly and invalid active-primary state cannot silently renew a serving lease.

Regression coverage was updated in `active_heartbeat_accepts_metadata_progress_after_peering`: the mismatched Active primary heartbeat now fails through `refresh_node_heartbeat`, leaves the previous lease deadline unchanged, and still allows a later valid progressed proof to renew service. Verification for the resolution:
- `cargo test -p storage control_plane -- --nocapture`
- `cargo nextest run` passed 5590 tests.

