## Report
Validated the finding against commit 9123ccc647a9e524e6e7304732018fc5b6ac6764 with a targeted Rust unit-test PoC in crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs. Code review confirmed the vulnerable chain: validate_pg_heartbeat_observations at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:4840-4867 only rejects duplicate/unknown/out-of-acting-set PG observations; should_record_pg_heartbeat_observation at :4869-4893 returns false for an Active primary observation with pending metadata command or a metadata proof below the active floor; heartbeat processing at :2047-2055 silently continues instead of returning an error, then commits the heartbeat and computes HeartbeatLease.serving from node-level state at :2075-2085; active_pg_route_for_storage_node_refresh at :390-420 treats a missing Active observation from the refreshing primary as handoff and returns an Active route with Some(primary_lease_deadline_ms). The passing PoC establishes PG 910 Active with accepted proof index 42, sends an Active primary heartbeat with bad proof index 41, and observed: `POC: lease_serving=true observation_recorded=false route_state=Active route_primary=1 route_deadline=Some(2120)`. This proves the bad observation was dropped, the node lease was renewed as serving, and refresh returned an Active route with a serving deadline to the same primary. A regression-style crash/assertion PoC expecting the safe invariant fails with `BUG: invalid active-primary heartbeat renewed a serving node lease`. Valgrind was attempted but unavailable (`bash: command not found: valgrind`). LLDB was used non-interactively and stopped at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:414 in active_pg_route_for_storage_node_refresh, with a backtrace through refresh_node_heartbeat -> runtime_map_for_storage_node_refresh -> pg_routes_for_storage_node_refresh -> active_pg_route_for_storage_node_refresh, confirming the Active route return path during the PoC.

